        "titulo": "Saying what hurts, step by step",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: to say what HURTS, use «wehtun» (separable) with the DATIVE of the person: «Der Kopf tut mir weh» (my head hurts). In English the body part is the subject and “my” shows whose it is; German adds the person in the dative. STEP 2: plural: «Die Füße tun mir weh.» STEP 3: ask «Was tut Ihnen weh?» or «Wo tut es weh?» STEP 4: another way, with «-schmerzen» (pains): «Ich habe Kopfschmerzen / Bauchschmerzen / Halsschmerzen / Rückenschmerzen.» STEP 5: «weh» also forms «Es tut weh» (it hurts) without the person. STEP 6: remember the reflexive dative from lesson 38: «Ich habe mir die Hand verletzt» (I hurt my hand), a form much used in the Perfekt.",
